    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (the only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**What the rule does:** when a new owner is *not* a hard duplicate (its `identityKey` doesn't collide) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while having a *different* telephone, the owner is still created and flagged with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id. Otherwise `possibleDuplicate` is `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted fields `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) with `@Column` mappings and accessors.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `possibleDuplicateOf(Owner)` helper (case-insensitive `lastName`, exact `postcode`, differing normalized telephone; picks the smallest-id match for determinism, returns null when the owner has no postcode), and wired it into `addOwner` after the hard-duplicate check so the two fields are set before save.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two `readOnly` properties to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them (MapStruct maps them by name).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns. The test profile (`hsqldb`) uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required there.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and the full suite builds green.",
